{"id":"h121","run":2,"role":"test_right","category":"simpleqa","question":"What is the name of the dedicated infrared flash used to project invisible infrared light onto the user's face to properly read the 30,000 facial points? Is the answer \"Flood Illuminator\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"OpenAI SimpleQA (openai/simple-evals, simple_qa_test_set.csv)","claims":[{"text":"Apple's TrueDepth system for Face ID includes an infrared flood illuminator.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.8,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The flood illuminator floods the face with invisible infrared light so the IR camera can capture an image in darkness or varied lighting.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The flood illuminator works like a flash, providing even infrared illumination.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.8,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The roughly 30,000 points are produced by the dot projector, not the flood illuminator.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The IR camera reads the dot pattern to build a depth map.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"If the question's 30,000 points clause identifies the dot-projecting component, the answer would be dot projector rather than flood illuminator.","confidence":0.4,"lean":-0.7,"theta":0.6283,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The question's description of a dedicated infrared flash projecting invisible IR light matches the flood illuminator's role.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.9,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The dot-projector detail is a mismatch in the question's wording, not evidence that another component is the infrared flash.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.8,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-0.0},{"text":"The answer to the question is yes, Flood Illuminator.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6